sequenceDiagram
    participant Scheduler as Invoice Expiration<br/>Scheduler
    participant Service as Invoice Expiration<br/>Service
    participant DB as Supabase<br/>Database
    participant SM as Payment State<br/>Machine
    participant Email as Email<br/>Service
    participant User as User

    Note over Scheduler: Every 5 minutes
    Scheduler->>Service: checkExpiredInvoices()

    Service->>Service: Check if already running
    alt Check already in progress
        Service-->>Scheduler: Return empty result
    else Lock acquired
        Service->>DB: Query expired payments<br/>WHERE state = 'PENDING'<br/>AND expires_at < NOW()
        DB-->>Service: Return expired payments

        loop For each expired payment
            Service->>SM: transition(paymentId, EXPIRED, metadata)
            SM->>DB: BEGIN TRANSACTION
            SM->>DB: UPDATE payments SET state = 'expired'
            SM->>DB: INSERT INTO payment_events
            SM->>DB: COMMIT TRANSACTION
            DB-->>SM: Transaction successful
            SM-->>Service: Transition result

            Service->>Email: sendInvoiceExpiredEmail(userId, paymentId, details)
            Email->>Email: Render template with data
            Email->>Email: Send via email provider
            alt Email sent successfully
                Email-->>Service: Success
                Service->>User: 📧 Invoice Expired Notification
                Service->>Service: Increment success count
            else Email failed
                Email-->>Service: Error
                Service->>Service: Log error & increment failed count
            end
        end

        Service->>Service: Update metrics<br/>- totalChecks++<br/>- totalExpired += count<br/>- lastCheckAt = now<br/>- lastCheckDuration = duration
        Service->>Service: Release lock
        Service-->>Scheduler: Check result<br/>(found, expired, failed counts)
    end

    Note over Scheduler: Schedule next check<br/>in 5 minutes
